      "content": "Test coverage gap: the loop only exercises widths 320 and 1024, but `AppWindowSizeClass.fromWidth` treats the expanded threshold inclusively (`width \u003e= style.wideLayoutMinWidth`, default 840). An off-by-one regression in the breakpoint (`\u003e` vs `\u003e=`) would not be caught. Consider adding a boundary case at exactly `Size(840, 760)` expecting the two-column layout.\n\nAlso, these assertions only check that the expected ledger keys are present. Since the continuous/primary/local ledgers are meant to be mutually exclusive, add `findsNothing` checks for the alternate keys in each branch (e.g. at 320 assert `settings-primary-ledger`/`settings-local-ledger` are absent, and vice versa at 1024) so a future refactor that renders both layouts simultaneously is caught.",
