      "thinking": "Alright. All `topRule` references have been removed. This section is consistent.\n\nNext, let me finalize my findings. The main concerns I'm seeing:\n\n1. **Missing `crossAxisAlignment: CrossAxisAlignment.stretch`** on the inner `Column` of the appearance-language section — inconsistent with all other Columns in this file. Under loose width constraints, the Column shrink-wraps to the widest child, so if `FSelectMenuTile`/`FAlert` shrink-wrap, the bottom divider `Border` (whose size matches the content) might not span the full section width. Low risk if forui's tiles expand, but worth adding for consistency and robustness. Severity: medium or low. This divider is the only separator between the appearance row and the language row within the shared bordered section, so a partial-width divider would be a visible defect. I'll rate this as medium.\n\nActually, wait. Let me reconsider whether the inner Column really receives loose width. Chain: `_SettingsSection.build` → Column(stretch) → DecoratedBox → child (inner Column). The stretch Column passes tight width [W, W] to the DecoratedBox. DecoratedBox passes the same constraints [W, W] to its child → inner Column receives tight width W. A Column with tight width W lays out children with cross-axis constraints... in the RenderFlex case: the constraints passed to children have the cross-axis loosened? Let me recall: `RenderFlex.performLayout` — for each child, cross-axis constraints: in the case of `CrossAxisAlignment.stretch` → tight; otherwise → loose `[0, crossMax]`, where crossMax = the flex's cross constraint's maxWidth. Inner Column receives tight [W,W] → maxWidth = W → children receive loose [0, W] cross-axis (since inner Column's own crossAxisAlignment is center (default)).\n\nSo DecoratedBox(appearance wrapper) receives loose [0, W], and ListenableBuilder(language) receives loose [0, W]. Then each section's stretch Column receives loose [0, W] and shrink-wraps to the widest child's width. If FTile-based widgets expand to fill their offered width (which is common — tiles typically use `width: double.infinity` or `SizedBox.expand` semantics), then child width = W → Column width W → all good.\n\nForui's FTile: In the forui library, `FTile` is typically built with `mergeSemantics` and a `Column`/`Row` inside a `DecoratedBox` with the group's decoration. I think forui tiles expand to fill available width (like list tiles). FAlert is also full-width. So in practice it's probably fine.\n\nStill, being explicit here is cheap and matches the file's convention, so I'll comment with low severity. Hmm, but I should be careful not to be too nitpicky. The review checklist values correctness. This is a latent robustness issue — okay, one low-severity comment.\n\n2. Another thing I noticed: `_SettingsValueRow` has `selected: true` — a check icon is always shown on the model row, and the semantics announce it as \"selected\". Fine by design.\n\n3. Another potential concern: **`_SettingsTileGroup` passes `const FTileGroupStyleDelta.delta(decoration: DecorationDelta.value(ShapeDecoration(shape: RoundedRectangleBorder())))`** — this replaces the decoration entirely. If the default group decoration included a background color (e.g., `FColors...`), the tiles might become transparent against the page background. Intentional per the design (the flat ledger look with only horizontal dividers). Skip.\n\n4. **Two hairlines around the spacing between sections** — skip (design).\n\n5. Now — wait, there's one more thing I should re-check: `_DiagnosticsSection`'s `message.contains('失败')` — this is existing code (not new). Skip.\n\n6. `_ModelResourceLedger` — the new `FTile`'s `subtitle` concatenates language + size + version into a two-line string. Previously it was two separate Texts with different semantics? No problem.\n\n7. **`_OfflineResourcesSection`'s `loading: viewModel.isLoading`** — while loading with option == null, it shows progress. No problem.\n\n8. Check the `_StoragePriva