cySection`'s FAlert + retry button inside the bordered section — visual only.\n\nAnother potential concern: in `_body`, in the expanded two-column layout, `localSections` always begins with `_OfflineResourcesSection`. If `hasDataSections` is false, we never reach the Row branch. So the Row branch always has at least offline + one data section. No problem.\n\nAlso — the single-column `Align` branch: even when `hasDataSections` is true, it merges everything; the keys 'settings-primary-ledger'/'settings-local-ledger' are not present; tests check 'settings-continuous-ledger'. No problem.\n\nI also want to re-check the interaction between `viewModel.errorMessage` and `_MeetingDefaultsSection`'s `loading` — no coupling. No problem.\n\nNow, test coverage: new tests cover language save failure rollback, theme save failure rollback, error message placement, responsive ledger keys, and maintained scale tests. Coverage is good. The existing tests for recording input / offline resources / diagnostics are maintained (not removed, though the largeText assertion for model-resource-name/status was relaxed — it became just findsOneWidget instead of a vertical stacking assertion; acceptable given the tile-based layout).\n\nOkay — one more real edge case I want to examine: **`onChange` of `managedRadio` when the menu is closed without selection** — nothing happens. No problem.\n\n**Edge: `values.firstOrNull` when values has two or more items** — a radio cannot have multiple. No problem.\n\nAnother subtle point — **`viewModel.select(mode)` when `mode == selectedMode` returns early**, but the radio control already reflects the tap; no change → consistent.\n\nAnother subtle point — **initial value of `saveFailed`**: `_FakeLanguagePreferences(failSave: true)`; `select` sets `_saveFailed = false` at the start and true on failure. On subsequent successful save, `_saveFailed = false` → alert disappears. Good.\n\nTheme: `_errorMessage` is set to null at the start of the next save. Good.\n\nFinal check for unused `appStyle` in `_AppearanceSection` — it's used in `SizedBox(height: appStyle.spaceMd)`. Also used in `_LanguageSection`. No problem.\n\nFinal verdict: only one modest finding (missing stretch). Also, the `BoxDecoration` for the divider's color/width might be worth mentioning — no, it's fine.\n\nActually, hold on. Let me look at the inner Column once more:\n\n```dart\nchild: Column(\n  children: [\n    if (themeSettings != null) DecoratedBox(...),\n    if (languageSettings != null) ListenableBuilder(...),\n  ],\n),\n```\n\nIf both are non-null: children = [DecoratedBox(theme), ListenableBuilder(language)]. Even if each child ends up full-width W, with the default center alignment — full-width children are centered — visually identical. The only risk is shrink-wrapping children. As analyzed, probably fine. Okay, low severity.\n\nHmm, one more — let me re-check the `Border` of the appearance wrapper's `BoxDecoration`: `Border(bottom: BorderSide(color: context.theme.colors.border, width: appStyle.dividerWidth))`. Meanwhile, `_SettingsSection` wraps everything with a symmetric horizontal border. So between the appearance row and the language row there's this bottom border; above the appearance row is the section's top border; below the language row is the section's bottom border. Consistent.\n\nBut note: the DecoratedBox's border is drawn around the appearance row's box, but if the appearance content has an error FAlert, the divider sits below the alert — good.\n\nNow — final scan for the diff's \"2.0 font scaling must not overflow\" requirement: `_SettingsValueRow` is now an FTile — kit handles it. `_ModelResourceStatus`'s Row(min) is in details — the kit handles it. Scale tests exist. No problem.\n\nAlso let me re-check whether anything else in the repo was referencing the removed `_DataLedger` or `_ModelResourceHeader` — they're private (underscore), only within this file. No problem.\n\nAnd confirm the deletion of 'language-section-title'... test still finds the `language-section` key — exists in the Column. The `appearance-section` key — exists. No problem.\n\nNow let me write the review comment. I have one solid medium/low comment. One more thing worth flagging: the `style: .delta(...)` blocks are duplicated verbatim across both sections — could be extracted into a shared constant for maintainability. This is a minor maintainability nit (style duplication in `_SettingsTileGroup` too). Might be able to bundle into a single low-severity maintainability comment. Let me phrase it as: identical style delta blocks in both sections; consider extracting a shared const. Actually, `const` dot shorthand expressions — can they be extracted into a `const`? Something like `const FSelectMenuTileStyleDelta.delta(...)`. Probably possible. I'll mention it briefly.\n\nTo summarize:\n1. Medium/low: The inner Column of the appearance-language section is missing `crossAxisAlignment: CrossAxisAlignment.stretch` — inconsistent with all other Columns in this file; if the tile/alert shrink-wraps under loose constraints, the section width and the divider between the appearance/language rows could shrink to content width. Add stretch for consistency and robustness.\n2. Low (maintainability): The duplicated `.delta(...)` style blocks across the language and appearance sections; extract into a shared constant.\n\nBoth comments will target new code lines in the diff.\n\nFor comment 1, the existing_code should be the Column in the diff:\n\n```dart\n          child: Column(\n            children: [\n```\n\nFor comment 2:\n\n```dart\n          style: .delta(\n            tileStyle: .delta(\n              contentDecoration: .delta([\n                .all(.shapeDelta(shape: const RoundedRectangleBorder())),\n              ]),\n            ),\n          ),\n```\n\nin `_LanguageSection` (first occurrence).\n\nLet me finalize.",
